INSTALL — cngpt build and installation instructions

QUICK START
-----------

  autoreconf -fi
  ./configure
  make
  make check
  sudo make install

DEPENDENCIES
------------

Required:
  - GCC (or compatible C11 compiler)
  - GNU autoconf >= 2.69
  - GNU automake >= 1.14
  - libopenblas-dev (provides cblas.h and libopenblas.so)
  - libm, libpthread (standard on Linux)

On Debian/Ubuntu:
  sudo apt-get install autoconf automake libopenblas-dev

Optional (for weight export):
  - Python 3.8+
  - pip install torch transformers

CONFIGURE OPTIONS
-----------------

  --prefix=DIR          Install files in DIR (default: /usr/local)
  --with-blas-cflags=F  CFLAGS for BLAS headers (auto-detected on Debian)
  --with-blas-libs=L    LIBS for BLAS linking (auto-detected on Debian)

Example for a custom OpenBLAS installation:

  ./configure \
    BLAS_CFLAGS="-I/opt/OpenBLAS/include" \
    BLAS_LIBS="-L/opt/OpenBLAS/lib -lopenblas"

PERFORMANCE FLAGS
-----------------

For maximum inference speed on x86-64 with AVX2/FMA:

  ./configure CFLAGS="-O3 -march=native -ffast-math -funroll-loops"
  make

See tests/bench.sh for an automated compiler-flag sweep.

CROSS-COMPILATION
-----------------

  ./configure --host=aarch64-linux-gnu \
    CC=aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc \
    BLAS_CFLAGS="-I/path/to/aarch64/openblas/include" \
    BLAS_LIBS="-L/path/to/aarch64/openblas/lib -lopenblas"

INSTALLATION LOCATIONS
----------------------

  Binary:   $prefix/bin/cngpt
  Manpage:  $prefix/share/man/man1/cngpt.1

To uninstall:
  sudo make uninstall
